  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="45">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 45</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.20"/><pb n="517" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne nul achat le vailiant de IIII den., ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.21"/> mort ne vif, sans testimonie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.22"/> ad IIII hommes u de bur[c<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.23"/>] u de vile.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="517" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne quis aliquid sine testibus emat. Nemo emat uel uiuum uel mortuum ad ualentiam IIII denar., sine IIII testibus aut de burgo aut de uilla campestri.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="45" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="272" ed="#robertson"/>Ne nul achat le vailiant de IIII den., ne mort ne vif, sans testimonie ad IIII hommes u de bur[c] u de vile.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="517" ed="#liebermann"/>45. <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#LeisWl_45.lnote.de1.g"/>Und niemand kaufe einen Werthgegenstand von 4 Pfennigen, weder lebloses noch lebendiges, ohne [dass] er als Zeugniss 4 Männer von Stadt oder Dorf hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">45. And let no one buy an object of value of 4 pennies, either inanimate or living, without [his] having as testimony 4 men from town or village.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="273" ed="#robertson"/>No-one shall buy anything 4 pence in value, either livestock or other property, unless he has 4 men as witnesses either from a town or a village.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="517"><ref target="clause:IICn_24">II Cn 24</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 24</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 272–273 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 517, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XLIII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XLIII. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">de m. vif <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">de m. vif Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">testemoine <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">testemoine Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">burt <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">burt I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_45.lnote.de1.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">anders über Gewährzug o.</hi> 21 <hi rend="italic">ff.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">otherwise on vouching to warranty above 21 ff.</seg></note>
      </div>
